                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0343e24d-d55e-3cd7-bd3b-13d3378a626a",
                        "entry_id": "6ddb4e87-0cd1-3a50-aec8-0ab53ce95815",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A heptomino shaped like the lowercase letter h, critical as a methuselah."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e85bf44c-5d7d-407c-8616-d9442a9c42e5",
                                "sense_id": "0343e24d-d55e-3cd7-bd3b-13d3378a626a",
                                "text": "This Herschel could be sent through stages of Buckingham's components, producing an arbitrary excess of gliders along a variety of different paths."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8980e954-f5cb-4cdd-94f4-0a70cef4dd96",
                                "sense_id": "0343e24d-d55e-3cd7-bd3b-13d3378a626a",
                                "text": "This uses Paul Callahan's catalysis of a glider into a Herschel and a glider, followed by David Buckingham's 77, 64, 64, 77, and 77 gen Herschel moves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c7ad804-0cec-4b9a-a465-2d6109be4836",
                                "sense_id": "0343e24d-d55e-3cd7-bd3b-13d3378a626a",
                                "text": "In Conway's Life, for example, a surprising number of small patterns serendipitously create R-pentominos and/or B-heptominos, which are \"tamable\" and happen to travel very well; this is what allows Herschel circuitry to be built."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
